Do not perform the proposed one-off three-chat capability refresh yet.

Continue the existing Mission Control controller task with this Chat-authored correction:

1. Repair the expired-controller-cycle generating condition. The current controller leaves an expired cycle nonterminal in its prior WAIT\_\* state because COMPLETE is effectively its only successful terminal step. Implement the smallest truthful terminalization mechanism for an expired cycle, preserving all historical send/admission/artifact evidence. A terminalized expired cycle must not block a genuinely fresh cycle, and a late artifact must not revive it.
2. Fail closed where terminalization is not safe. In particular, reconcile and preserve any ambiguous/crossed send or unresolved admission before terminalization. Add focused regressions for:
   - expired WAIT cycle becomes terminal and no longer monopolizes fresh-cycle admission;
   - terminalization is idempotent;
   - late artifact cannot resume an expired cycle;
   - unresolved/ambiguous send state cannot be silently erased;
   - completed cycles remain unchanged.
3. Treat the newly asserted requirement for “current capability receipts for all three non-production chats” as a follow-up requirement-accretion question, not an accepted prerequisite. Re-bind it to the current owner requirement: one successful fresh PM-mediated controller fixture at the real consumer seam.

Determine exactly what failure each fresh capability receipt prevents that is not already covered by the existing exact MC\_ONLY registration, automation-owned target/window binding, provider-session binding, account/session checks, and fail-closed destination validation.

4. If the three-receipt gate is not necessary to prevent a material unsafe action, remove it as a prerequisite and let the real fresh fixture provide the direct capability evidence.

If some freshness check is genuinely necessary, implement the smallest lifecycle mechanism instead:

- invalidate only on a concrete relevant change;
- refresh automatically under existing Mission Control authority;
- use a new single-use challenge when required; never replay a historical challenge;
- cache the valid receipt until an actual invalidator occurs;
- do not ask the owner to repeatedly authorize routine refresh;
- stop for the owner only on a genuine login/MFA/wrong-account/missing-chat/security boundary.

5. Do not send any live capability probe merely to satisfy the old blocker while doing this repair. First establish whether the gate is necessary.

Use GPT-5.6 Sol; no Astra escalation is warranted unless execution evidence shows a genuine reasoning shortfall.

Produce the smallest reviewable PR with focused tests and a plain-English receipt. Do not merge it yourself. After the candidate is ready, return:\
Goal / Where we are / Next needed / Your action.

The intended next live action after an accepted repair is the already-authorized single fresh PM-mediated fixture, not a new chain of preflight proofs.
